# Docs — only track Logs/, Sessions/, Deferred.md (Plan/Changelog/Doclog/Audit
# stay local-only by deliberate policy). NOT blanket-ignoring Docs/ here — that
# would also hide the tracked Docs/Sessions, Docs/Logs, Docs/Deferred.md this
# repo intentionally commits. Left as-is on purpose (Task 8 follow-up).
Docs/Changelog
Docs/Doclog
Docs/Audit/
Docs/**/*.png
Docs/**/*.jpg
Docs/**/*.jpeg
Docs/Plan
Matrix/

# Internal security-architecture docs — never belong in a public clone.
# These ARE currently tracked in THIS repo (a .gitignore rule does not
# untrack an already-tracked file), so this is a no-op here; it becomes a
# real guard the moment a future dev clone (Task 9's published repo) drops
# a fresh CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md in place and runs `git add -A`.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md

# Runtime data (personal, rebuildable, or ephemeral)
tesseract/provisional/
tesseract/logs/
tesseract/telegram/
tesseract/sessions/
tesseract/agent-state/
# Operator's live workspace/memory-store/vault/tars-workshop are private and
# never ship (SOUL.md, DIARY.md, MEMORY.md, real memories, real vault docs,
# real workshop artifacts, ...). `_shipping/` in each is the hand-authored
# neutral-scaffold exception — same pattern across all four — tracked so the
# builder can seed a fresh install ready-to-use instead of empty/crashing on
# a missing dir (Task 11f for workspace; Task 17 for the other three).
tesseract/workspace/*
!tesseract/workspace/_shipping/
!tesseract/workspace/_shipping/**
tesseract/memory-store/*
!tesseract/memory-store/_shipping/
!tesseract/memory-store/_shipping/**
tesseract/vault/*
!tesseract/vault/_shipping/
!tesseract/vault/_shipping/**
tesseract/tars-workshop/*
!tesseract/tars-workshop/_shipping/
!tesseract/tars-workshop/_shipping/**

